# The Aether release aeb's OWN machinery is built against.
#
# This is NOT the Aether that compiles your program — that one is yours,
# resolved from $AETHER / PATH, and aeb never touches it. This pin is only
# for compiling `.foo.ae` build files into aeb's orchestrator, and is an
# implementation detail of this aeb release (like the gcc that built your
# `make` binary).
#
# aeb fetches this version into its own cache on first use if the ae on
# PATH is older. See asks/two-aethers-pinned-toolchain-vs-declared-dep.md
#
# One bare version string. Bump when aeb starts calling a primitive that
# an older Aether lacks (e.g. os.spawn_proc needed 0.442,
# os.wait_any_timeout needed 0.447, string.replace_all needed 0.463).
#
# This is a FLOOR, not a preference: it is the oldest Aether that can
# compile aeb's own sources. Anything newer on PATH is accepted as-is.
# Keep it at the real requirement — raising it to chase a nicer release
# forces a needless fetch on everyone sitting between the two versions.
#
# SEPARATE CONCERN — glibc. Releases up to ~0.449 were built on
# ubuntu-latest and carry a GLIBC_2.38 floor, so `aetherc` dies on Debian
# 12 (glibc 2.36) while `ae --version` still works. Aether's release.yml
# now pins ubuntu-22.04 (glibc 2.35) and 0.452.0 measures at GLIBC_2.34.
# That affects WHICH RELEASE TO FETCH when the pin is not satisfied, not
# what the floor is — so it belongs in the fetch logic, not here.
0.463.0
